      {
        "id": "1lEgWRFYh9E68mEE",
        "title": "Investigating",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>By now you have a first prototype of a prosthesis, you have figured out how to make an automatic machine, and you have figured out how to make a servo work.</p><p>Today, you&#x27;ll figure out how to connect your prosthesis to a servo so that it makes motions automatically.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Knn6rLiLh3ahAfja",
        "title": "You might want to enlarge this!",
        "content": {
          "type": "Image",
          "url": "vibe/images/Icon-Enlarge-Lessons.png",
          "filename": "vibe/images/Icon-Enlarge-Lessons.png"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "6N-AL8wb2xZiEdcU",
        "title": "Inspiration from Nature",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>A lot of robots are made of hard materials.</p><p>Hard robots are good for a lot of things, and they are used in a lot of places, like in healthcare, manufacturing, and even in music and art contexts!</p><p>But, they are not so good at holding some kinds of delicate objects, like a raw egg or a live mouse.</p><p>Scientists at the Whitesides Research Group at Harvard University were inspired by animals - like starfish and elephant trunks - to make soft robots.</p><p>They aren&#x27;t just inspired by the shapes in nature, but also the materials. Plants, DNA, and natural rubber all use materials called polymers.</p><p>The Whitesides scientists are developing synthetic polymers that are rubbery and elastic, like materials in nature. </p><p>Look at one of the robots they designed, and how it compares to a starfish! </p>"
          ]
        }
      },
